<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27331" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lychnis</span></b> , ĭdis, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adj. f.</i>, =
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λυχνίς</span>, <i>lightgiving, shining</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: lychnides puellae, <i>girls with lamps</i>, Fulg. Myth. prooem.
			1.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lychnis</span></b> , ĭdis, f.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A kind of rose of a fiery red</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 21, 4,
				10, § 18</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Lychnis agria, another plant, <i><span class="en">Plin. 25,
				10, 80, § 129</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<i>A gem of a fiery color</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 37,
				7, 29, § 103</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
